"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"vOLWw1s8ndtZY8TPj4Q2O","photo_date":"2015-03-03T11:33:57.000Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T11:34:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/U2oMy7a7hyt7mVvreLAWu","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/U2oMy7a7hyt7mVvreLAWu"}},{"id":"lwbwyd3rn08RCaImaiSZ4","ext":"jpg","post_id":"5xoKhKkOrLoVgo1L3emUk","description":"","caption":"The Horn","poi_name":null,"subject":"Eric Bessette","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"vOLWw1s8ndtZY8TPj4Q2O","photo_date":"2015-03-03T11:33:57.000Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T11:34:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/lwbwyd3rn08RCaImaiSZ4","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/lwbwyd3rn08RCaImaiSZ4"}},{"id":"889825","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892359","description":"Darren Dangerdeeds on the biggest play wave on the run, Bus Stop.  Around 22' on the gauge.","caption":"Bus Stop","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Emile Elliott","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/889825","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/889825"}},{"id":"3VVIYZuGJXKKhgPxLFaL2","ext":"jpg","post_id":"5xoKhKkOrLoVgo1L3emUk","description":"","caption":"Deadwood County Park Put-in","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"109218","photo_date":"2015-03-03T11:33:57.000Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T11:34:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3VVIYZuGJXKKhgPxLFaL2","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3VVIYZuGJXKKhgPxLFaL2"}}],"detail":{"id":"1524","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Lake Creek is known as one of the region's top playboating destinations when the water is high. This run can also be enjoyed as a class II/III run at lower flows.\n\nAt high flows swims are often long and dangerous, so make sure that roll is bomber.\n\nAccess Logistics:\n\nLake Creek has easy access off Highway 36. You have a few put-in options depending on how much warm up you want before the big drops. The top put-in is in Deadwood at the county park across from the post office at highway mile 13.3. Another access is an informal free parking area at the Green Creek confluence at highway mile 12.2. If you want to put in just above the main rapids, Schindler County Park at highway mile 10.5 is also an option.\n\nYou can scout the Horn, the big drop on the run, from the pull-out at highway mile 9.2\n\nIf you want to end your trip on Lake Creek you can take-out just upstream of the confluence with the Siuslaw. To reach this site, turn on to Stagecoach Road at Highway 36 mile 8.4. Head 0.1 mile over the bridge across Lake Creek and turn upstream on the drive to Konnie Memorial ODFW fishing access site. It's 0.5 mile upstream on this drive to the river access point.\n\nMost continue on downstream on the Siuslaw River. You can take-out at mile 5.7 on Highway 36 at the Tide Wayside County Park, or continue down to mile 4.5 or 4.3 to free informal access sites.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"5.3","correlations":[{"reachID":"1524","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":"Not the play run of high water but still a fun river trip.","mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"5","beginMediumRunnable":"7","beginHighRunnable":"12","endHighRunnable":"22"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SIUSLAW RIVER NEAR MAPLETON, OR","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"14307620","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"526","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4.03